      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "d0333656d784ef27b2aee1e5d09cfe46b9040c8a97d7aecc88164b78f176ab6c"
    },
    {
      "type": "proposition",
      "content": "However, Equation 23.29 carries the unstated assumption that the environmental variance, $ \\sigma_e^2 $, is unchanged over levels of inbreeding, which may not be correct (Chapter 17). More generally, $ \\sigma_e^2 $ can be replaced by $ \\sigma_e^2(t) $ to accommodate this concern. Note that any initial contribution to the selection response from dominance will quickly decay (as $ 2^{-n} $).",
      "source_page": 828,
